---
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { contact, legal } from '../config';
---

<LegalPage
  title="Privacy notice"
  kicker="Privacy"
  description="How PlayRun handles the details you send through the contact form, what the site stores in your browser, and your rights under UK GDPR."
  lead="This site collects very little. Here is exactly what, why, where it goes, and how long I keep it."
>
  <section class="row">
    <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
    <p>
      The controller is {legal.controller}{legal.address ? `, ${legal.address}` : `, ${contact.location}`}. Email{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a> for anything in this notice.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="row">
    <h2>The contact form</h2>
    <p>
      When you send a message I receive your name, your email address, the message itself, the address of the page
      you sent it from and the time you sent it. I use these only to reply to you.
    </p>
    <p>The lawful basis is my legitimate interest in answering people who write to me.</p>
    <p>
      The form delivers the message into my Google Workspace account: Gmail, a Google Sheet and the Apps Script that
      connects them. Google processes that data on my behalf under its Workspace terms.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="row">
    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>
      The site is hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub may log the IP address of each request for security, under its own
      privacy statement. The fonts are served from this site. There are no third-party requests, apart from the
      contact form, which is sent to my Google Workspace. There are no analytics and no cookies.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="row">
    <h2>What the site stores in your browser</h2>
    <p>
      The games on the site keep their progress in your browser's local storage: the bugs you have caught, the
      achievements you have unlocked and whether the games are on or off. This never leaves your browser and is never
      sent to me. The Reset button in the HUD clears it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="row">
    <h2>How long I keep it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Messages in my records are deleted after 24 months.</li>
      <li>Nothing else is collected, so there is nothing else to keep.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="row">
    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      You can ask for a copy of the personal data I hold about you, ask me to correct or delete it, and object to how I
      use it. Email <a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a> and I will answer. If you are not happy with
      my answer you can complain to the Information Commissioner's Office at{' '}
      <a href="https://ico.org.uk/" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</LegalPage>
